    {
      "id": "03-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new Quotation. Set the Customer to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' — this is an autocomplete dropdown field, so you must select the option from the dropdown that appears, not merely type the name. Add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again via the autocomplete dropdown, choosing an actual option), and set the Quantity to 3. Do not add any other lines. Save the quotation (do NOT confirm it yet). Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the Unit Price the app automatically filled in for that line, (c) the Untaxed amount the app computes for the quotation, and (d) the quotation's reference/name if shown. Do not wait for network idle — the app long-polls; wait for concrete page elements.",
